WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.316 --> 00:00:12.881
Hello, everyone.

2
00:00:13.181 --> 00:00:13.842
It's Melissa.

3
00:00:14.662 --> 00:00:16.423
Today was Bring-Your-Child-to-Work day.

4
00:00:17.404 --> 00:00:22.587
So instead of going to school, I went with my mom to her workplace—a big bank on Wall

5
00:00:22.627 --> 00:00:23.828
Street in New York City.

6
00:00:24.628 --> 00:00:27.350
It was really fun but pretty tiring too!

7
00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:33.073
My mom told me some cool things about Wall Street today, but I had already learned some facts

8
00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:33.573
from Mr.

9
00:00:33.613 --> 00:00:34.894
Fay's landmarks lesson.

10
00:00:35.854 --> 00:00:41.036
Mr. Fay told us that the area called Wall Street is located at the southern end of Manhattan.

11
00:00:41.896 --> 00:00:44.317
It's also one of the world's busiest financial centers.

12
00:00:45.058 --> 00:00:49.199
In fact, millions of dollars are traded there every single day!

13
00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.001
Wall Street has been around for hundreds of years.

14
00:00:53.941 --> 00:00:59.804
In 1653 the lower end of Manhattan Island was a Dutch settlement called New Amsterdam.

15
00:01:00.684 --> 00:01:06.370
But British colonists wanted the land too, so the Dutch built a wooden wall to protect themselves from

16
00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.231
possible attack.

17
00:01:08.292 --> 00:01:12.916
Near the wall was a path, which eventually became known as "Wall Street."

18
00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:14.618
We asked Mr.

19
00:01:14.658 --> 00:01:18.622
Fay how this narrow path grew into such a mighty symbol of financial power.

20
00:01:19.603 --> 00:01:24.828
He said that in the late 1700s, New York City was a main center of trading and commerce.

21
00:01:25.656 --> 00:01:31.038
Back then a small group of traders used to meet under a buttonwood tree at 68 Wall Street

22
00:01:31.058 --> 00:01:33.978
to trade stocks, or shares, of companies they owned.

23
00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:42.661
In 1792, 24 of these traders signed the Buttonwood Agreement, promising to trade stocks only with each other.

24
00:01:43.581 --> 00:01:46.462
They also set some basic rules for how trading should be done.

25
00:01:47.402 --> 00:01:52.064
In 1817 this group officially became the New York Stock and Exchange Board.

26
00:01:53.516 --> 00:01:56.218
Today it's known as the New York Stock Exchange.

27
00:01:57.318 --> 00:02:03.221
After the establishment of the New York Stock Exchange, more banks and financial institutions moved to the area.

28
00:02:04.122 --> 00:02:09.825
Eventually "Wall Street" came to mean not just the street but also the entire financial district in lower

29
00:02:09.865 --> 00:02:15.908
Manhattan. If you've ever been to Wall Street and the rest of the financial district, you know it's

30
00:02:15.928 --> 00:02:21.972
a busy place, with businesspeople darting in and out of subway stations and tall, shiny office buildings.

31
00:02:23.016 --> 00:02:27.119
As my mom and I walked around, she had to warn me several times to watch where I

32
00:02:27.159 --> 00:02:27.800
was going!

33
00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:34.105
Wall Street has lots of tall modern buildings, but there are also some older historic ones.

34
00:02:35.266 --> 00:02:41.711
First built in 1698, Trinity Church was one of the first church congregations established in America.

35
00:02:42.952 --> 00:02:48.957
Back when Manhattan was the nation's first capital, a building called Federal Hall housed the government offices.

36
00:02:50.038 --> 00:02:55.041
Federal Hall was where America's first president—George Washington—was sworn into office.

37
00:02:56.642 --> 00:03:01.925
I bet you've seen photos of a popular tourist attraction on Wall Street—the famous charging bull.

38
00:03:02.905 --> 00:03:10.069
Apparently an artist created this huge bronze statue in 1989 and installed it one winter night in front

39
00:03:10.109 --> 00:03:11.490
of the New York Stock Exchange.

40
00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:17.333
There was an economic recession going on at the time, and the artist wanted to cheer up discouraged

41
00:03:17.373 --> 00:03:17.973
New Yorkers.

42
00:03:19.014 --> 00:03:22.496
So he sculpted "Charging Bull" as a special holiday gift.

43
00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.503
My mom took my picture in front of the bull, and I rubbed its nose for good luck

44
00:03:27.783 --> 00:03:30.325
because it's supposed to represent financial prosperity.

45
00:03:30.345 --> 00:03:35.209
(Hey! Do you think my parents will finally raise my allowance now?)

46
00:03:37.571 --> 00:03:42.454
Throughout its history, Wall Street has been associated with America's wealth and prosperity.

47
00:03:43.335 --> 00:03:43.775
But Mr.

48
00:03:43.855 --> 00:03:49.600
Fay reminded us that Wall Street has also been associated with periods of economic decline.

49
00:03:50.612 --> 00:03:55.676
When the American stock market crashed in 1929, it triggered the Great Depression.

50
00:03:56.697 --> 00:04:02.082
Millions of people lost their jobs, and devastating poverty spread around the world.

51
00:04:03.143 --> 00:04:03.803
Another U.S.

52
00:04:03.823 --> 00:04:05.685
stock market crash came in 2008.

53
00:04:06.766 --> 00:04:13.151
A recession swept the globe, and many people blamed Wall Street for starting it by using risky lending

54
00:04:13.191 --> 00:04:14.732
practices to make lots of money.

55
00:04:15.733 --> 00:04:22.558
By 2011 the "Occupy" movement had sprung up, with people around the world occupying city parks to protest

56
00:04:22.638 --> 00:04:24.239
greed in the financial industry.

57
00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:31.563
As a symbol of wealth and prosperity, Wall Street has also been the target of violence.

58
00:04:31.703 --> 00:04:36.626
In 1920 a bomb exploded on a street corner, killing 38 people.

59
00:04:37.587 --> 00:04:42.830
In 1993 terrorists detonated a bomb in the World Trade Center's underground parking lot.

60
00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:50.872
Then, on September 11, 2001, terrorists flew two planes into the twin towers of the World Trade Center.

61
00:04:51.772 --> 00:04:55.696
The towers were destroyed, and thousands of people were murdered.

62
00:04:56.616 --> 00:05:02.922
Today at the World Trade Center site, there's a memorial, a museum, and a new tower where the

63
00:05:02.982 --> 00:05:03.802
two once stood.

64
00:05:04.783 --> 00:05:10.688
The new tower, known as One World Trade Center, is one of the tallest buildings in the world.

65
00:05:11.669 --> 00:05:17.649
At the memorial Mom and I walked around two square pools, reading the names of the victims written

66
00:05:17.689 --> 00:05:18.270
in stone.

67
00:05:19.831 --> 00:05:24.254
Today the New York Stock Exchange is one of the most famous places on Wall Street.

68
00:05:25.114 --> 00:05:27.996
In fact, it's the biggest stock exchange in the world.

69
00:05:28.937 --> 00:05:32.800
My mom took me there, and the building's entrance is as grand as Mr.

70
00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:33.740
Fay said it was.

71
00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:39.084
Six tall white columns support a giant marble sculpture over the doorway.

72
00:05:40.004 --> 00:05:43.066
We took a tour of the building and looked down on the trading floor.

73
00:05:43.907 --> 00:05:47.622
I've seen it before on TV, but it was pretty cool to see the real thing.

74
00:05:48.562 --> 00:05:53.346
The floor was buzzing with activity as traders ran around, shouting and making deals.

75
00:05:54.326 --> 00:05:59.250
I found out that each morning and afternoon, a bell is rung at the Stock Exchange to start

76
00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.471
and end the trading day.

77
00:06:02.032 --> 00:06:08.416
Celebrities are often invited to ring the bell, so it's been clanged by astronauts, storm troopers from Star

78
00:06:08.457 --> 00:06:12.439
Wars, rock stars, even a duck from a TV commercial!

79
00:06:14.104 --> 00:06:18.988
After our tour of the Stock Exchange, Mom and I left Wall Street and took the subway uptown.

80
00:06:19.928 --> 00:06:22.110
We met my dad for dinner at a fancy restaurant.

81
00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:24.111
That was really fun too.

82
00:06:25.052 --> 00:06:29.515
Well, I'd better get some rest now because tomorrow I'm not going back to Wall Street with my

83
00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:34.198
mom. I'm headed back to school—to take a big math test.

84
00:06:35.099 --> 00:06:36.500
Good night, Little Fox readers!
